error[Q0011]: numbers can't start with `0`
 --> example.ql:1:1
  |
1 | 00.5
  | ^^ leading zero
  |
  = note: a leading zero would mean an octal number in some languages, so Quell doesn't allow it
help: for the number 0, remove the leading zeros
  |
1 | 0.5
  |

=== 0x
error[Q0012]: `0x` must be followed by hex digits
 --> example.ql:1:1
  |
1 | 0x
  | ^^ no hex digits here
  |
  = help: a hex number uses the digits 0 to 9 and the letters a to f, as in `0xff`

=== 0b
error[Q0012]: `0b` must be followed by binary digits
 --> example.ql:1:1
  |
1 | 0b
  | ^^ no binary digits here
  |
  = help: a binary number uses only the digits 0 and 1, as in `0b1010`

=== 0o
error[Q0012]: `0o` must be followed by octal digits
 --> example.ql:1:1
  |
1 | 0o
  | ^^ no octal digits here
  |
  = help: an octal number uses only the digits 0 to 7, as in `0o17`

=== 0b102
error[Q0013]: `2` is not a binary digit
 --> example.ql:1:5
  |
1 | 0b102
  |     ^ a binary number uses only the digits 0 and 1
  |
help: for the decimal number 102, remove the `0b`
  |
1 | 102
  |

