=== \'\'
error[Q0020]: a character literal needs exactly one character
 --> example.ql:1:1
  |
1 | ''
  | ^^ nothing between the quotes
  |
  = help: put one character between the quotes, such as `'a'` or `' '`
help: for empty text, use a string
  |
1 | ""
  |

=== \'ab\'
error[Q0021]: single quotes hold exactly one character
 --> example.ql:1:1
  |
1 | 'ab'
  | ^^^^ this has more than one character
  |
help: for text, use double quotes
  |
1 | "ab"
  |

=== \'é\'
error[Q0021]: single quotes hold exactly one character
 --> example.ql:1:1
  |
1 | 'é'
  | ^^^^ this has more than one character
  |
  = note: this is a letter followed by separate accents, which together look like one character
help: write it as the single character `é`
  |
1 | 'é'
  |

=== \'a
error[Q0022]: this character literal is never closed
 --> example.ql:1:1
  |
1 | 'a
  | ^^ this character has no closing `'`
  |
help: add the closing `'`
  |
1 | 'a'
  |

=== \'
error[Q0022]: this character literal is never closed
 --> example.ql:1:1
  |
1 | '
  | ^ the line ends before the closing `'`
  |
  = help: a character literal is one character between single quotes, such as `'a'`

=== \'\n\'
error[Q0022]: this character literal is never closed
 --> example.ql:1:1
  |
1 | '
  | ^ the line ends before the closing `'`
  |
  = help: a character literal is one character between single quotes, such as `'a'`

error[Q0022]: this character literal is never closed
 --> example.ql:2:1
  |
2 | '
  | ^ the line ends before the closing `'`
  |
  = help: a character literal is one character between single quotes, such as `'a'`

=== \"\\q\"
error[Q0030]: `\q` is not an escape
 --> example.ql:1:2
  |
1 | "\q"
  |  ^^ unknown escape
  |
  = note: the escapes are `\n`, `\r`, `\t`, `\0`, `\\`, `\"`, `\'` and `\u{...}`
help: for a backslash, write it twice
  |
1 | "\\q"
  |

=== \"\\
error[Q0034]: this string is never closed
 --> example.ql:1:1
  |
1 | "\
  | ^ the file ends before the closing `"`
  |
  = note: a string can't hold a line break; write `\n` for one, or use a multi-line string that starts with `"""`
help: write the `\` twice and add `"` where the text ends
  |
1 | "\\"
  |

error[Q0030]: this `\` starts an escape, but the file ends here
 --> example.ql:1:2
  |
1 | "\
  |  ^ incomplete escape
  |
help: for a backslash, write `\\`
  |
1 | "\\
  |

=== \"\\{\"
error[Q0031]: there is no `\{` escape
 --> example.ql:1:2
  |
1 | "\{"
  |  ^^ not an escape
  |
help: in a string, a literal brace is written twice: `{{`
  |
1 | "{{"
  |

=== \'\\{\'
error[Q0031]: there is no `\{` escape
 --> example.ql:1:2
  |
1 | '\{'
  |  ^^ not an escape
  |
help: a brace needs no escape in a character literal: `'{'`
  |
1 | '{'
  |

=== \"\\u{}\"
error[Q0032]: `\u{...}` needs a hex number of 1 to 6 digits
 --> example.ql:1:2
  |
1 | "\u{}"
  |  ^^^^ invalid escape
  |
  = help: write the code of the character in hex, such as `\u{E9}` or `\u{1F600}`

=== \"\\uE9\"
error[Q0032]: `\u` must be followed by a hex code in braces
 --> example.ql:1:2
  |
1 | "\uE9"
  |  ^^ incomplete escape
  |
  = help: write the code of the character in hex, such as `\u{E9}` for `é`

=== \"\\u{E9\"
error[Q0032]: this `\u{` escape is missing its closing `}`
 --> example.ql:1:2
  |
1 | "\u{E9"
  |  ^^^^^ invalid escape
  |
help: add the `}`
  |
1 | "\u{E9}"
  |

=== \"\\u{1234567}\"
error[Q0032]: `\u{...}` takes at most 6 hex digits
 --> example.ql:1:2
  |
1 | "\u{1234567}"
  |  ^^^^^^^^^^^ invalid escape
  |
  = note: the largest character code is `10FFFF`
  = help: write the code of the character in hex, such as `\u{E9}` or `\u{1F600}`

=== \"\\u{xyz}\"
error[Q0032]: `\u{...}` needs a hex number of 1 to 6 digits
 --> example.ql:1:2
  |
1 | "\u{xyz}"
  |  ^^^^^^^ invalid escape
  |
  = help: write the code of the character in hex, such as `\u{E9}` or `\u{1F600}`

=== \"\\u{D800}\"
error[Q0033]: `\u{D800}` is not a Unicode character
 --> example.ql:1:2
  |
1 | "\u{D800}"
  |  ^^^^^^^^ no character has this code
  |
  = note: the codes from `D800` to `DFFF` are surrogates, which are not characters
  = help: check the code of the character you want

=== \"\\u{110000}\"
error[Q0033]: `\u{110000}` is not a Unicode character
 --> example.ql:1:2
  |
1 | "\u{110000}"
  |  ^^^^^^^^^^ no character has this code
  |
  = note: the largest character code is `10FFFF`
  = help: check the code of the character you want

